# ---- stashes window ---------------------------------------------------------
# A stash is work put away: the working tree as it was, saved and rolled back. The window is the
# list, what is in the stash on the row you are pointing at, and the one thing you create below it.
# The rule underneath it is that a row is addressed by a *position* -- stash@{1} is whatever happens
# to be second right now -- so FlickGit checks the stash is still the one on screen before it pops or
# drops anything. stash.moved is the other case.
#
# Drop takes several rows at once and asks once, with the totals. Pop takes one: popping several in
# a row is a chain of merges, where the second lands on a tree the first has already changed.
#
# There is no wording here for `stash clear` or `stash apply`, because neither is offered anywhere.

# {0} repository name
stash.title = Stashes — {0}
stash.new = Stash your changes
stash.message.label = Message — optional; without one, Git names the commit you were on
stash.untracked = Include untracked
